WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
This show contains scenes that some viewers may 
find disturbing.​ Viewer discretion ​is ​advised.

00:03.140 --> 00:07.640
<b>Heart of Darkness</b>

00:03.160 --> 00:05.570
So what are we going to do now?

00:05.570 --> 00:07.810
We're going to set traps and head up.

00:07.810 --> 00:08.940
Traps?

00:08.940 --> 00:10.450
You'll see in a second.

00:10.450 --> 00:12.630
But we're going up now?

00:13.050 --> 00:15.610
These goblins set up a base 
in a building like this.

00:15.610 --> 00:18.110
It's pretty easy to figure 
out what they're thinking.

00:18.660 --> 00:23.080
The most important one is going to be at 
either the very top or the very bottom.

00:23.510 --> 00:24.790
Ah...

00:25.070 --> 00:26.570
The only problem is the...

00:26.950 --> 00:28.830
Mokele Mubenbe?

00:28.830 --> 00:31.230
Would you remember it already?

00:31.230 --> 00:35.520
The problem is that the one controlling 
that thing is most likely a spellcaster.

00:40.170 --> 00:41.420
Are you all right?

00:41.420 --> 00:42.350
I'm fine.

00:42.350 --> 00:43.730
Thank goodness.

00:43.730 --> 00:47.770
Why didn't the ancients bother making a lift?

00:48.730 --> 00:49.430
Oh.

00:51.630 --> 00:54.060
It does seem to be moving.

00:54.430 --> 00:55.540
And yet...

00:56.590 --> 00:57.590
What's this?

00:58.340 --> 00:59.650
Ah, I see.

00:59.650 --> 01:02.800
This doesn't move by key. It moves by code.

01:04.040 --> 01:05.750
What about this?

01:06.100 --> 01:10.870
At first, I thought the numbers on 
here were just associated with the key.

01:10.870 --> 01:11.950
Give it a try.

01:12.530 --> 01:13.350
Okay.

01:27.490 --> 01:28.940
It looks like we were right.

01:29.160 --> 01:31.180
Do you think there are any traps?

01:31.180 --> 01:34.860
I'm sure it's not a simple enough setup 
that the goblins can mess around with it.

01:35.770 --> 01:36.830
Let's go.

01:37.530 --> 01:39.730
We must defeat the goblins.

01:40.400 --> 01:41.280
Yeah.

01:42.230 --> 01:44.360
We're going to slay all the goblins.

03:20.380 --> 03:21.410
Sorry...

03:21.930 --> 03:25.510
But also... thank you, everyone.

03:26.080 --> 03:30.580
I invited you all here for my sister's 
wedding, but it turned into this mess.

03:30.580 --> 03:32.730
Eh, it's no big deal.

03:33.110 --> 03:36.800
It feels great to make 
the elves owe me a debt.

03:37.390 --> 03:39.690
And well, you know...

03:40.570 --> 03:42.150
We're friends.

03:43.810 --> 03:47.890
You're always taking care of us, Lady Archer.

03:47.890 --> 03:49.950
This is nothing.

03:50.130 --> 03:51.610
Plus, you know...

03:51.610 --> 03:56.040
Any mention of goblins and 
Goblin Slayer will take off.

03:56.920 --> 03:57.970
Right?

03:58.620 --> 03:59.530
Yeah.

04:00.330 --> 04:01.800
For crying out loud...

04:02.970 --> 04:06.470
We've only been around each other 
for a little over a year,

04:06.830 --> 04:08.640
but you're all so weird.

04:08.640 --> 04:11.210
You'd better not forget me 
for at least a century.

04:11.210 --> 04:13.080
You dwarves are so dumb.

04:14.410 --> 04:17.030
Of course I'd never forget any of you.

04:24.510 --> 04:25.610
All right.

04:28.780 --> 04:31.520
I hear wind, footsteps, murmurings...

04:31.520 --> 04:33.350
Probably a roof or an arcade.

04:33.350 --> 04:34.500
There are a lot of them.

04:34.770 --> 04:36.720
I want to cut right through.

04:37.070 --> 04:37.960
What do you think?

04:39.070 --> 04:43.170
Why don't we go for the most 
orthodox method for now?

04:43.510 --> 04:45.550
Sir Goblin Slayer, you take the front.

04:45.550 --> 04:48.010
Sir Spellcaster and I will take both flanks.

04:48.460 --> 04:50.920
Lady Priestess, stay behind Lady Archer.

04:50.920 --> 04:52.130
U-Understood.

04:52.600 --> 04:57.150
So you just need me to look out in 
all directions and call out support.

04:57.150 --> 04:58.570
You are the key.

04:58.570 --> 05:00.070
I know.

05:00.070 --> 05:03.570
Good grief. I <i>am</i> a mage, you know.

05:03.570 --> 05:05.610
We're counting on you.

05:05.610 --> 05:07.110
Yes, yes, I know.

05:07.110 --> 05:10.400
I'll show you just how 
manly dwarven men can be.

05:12.210 --> 05:16.650
And we lizardmen are all noble warriors.

05:33.770 --> 05:34.810
You've got this?

05:37.750 --> 05:39.650
Yes, I can do this.

05:39.650 --> 05:41.720
Once we open this, 
we're going to run. Get ready.

05:41.720 --> 05:42.810
What about the spellcaster?

05:42.810 --> 05:45.610
If you find it, take it down first. 
That's the only choice we have.

05:45.610 --> 05:49.070
I know I'm stating the obvious, 
but what a pain in the ass.

05:49.070 --> 05:51.900
Even if it casts a spell 
that affects our status,

05:51.900 --> 05:54.410
if one of us can still move, 
you'll have to regroup.

05:54.860 --> 05:57.350
As long as we don't all go down, 
we'll have a plan.

05:57.350 --> 05:58.610
And if we all go down?

05:58.610 --> 05:59.500
Just don't.

06:01.410 --> 06:04.340
Well, all right. I'll do my best 
to make sure that doesn't happen.

06:04.340 --> 06:06.320
Yeah. Don't use any spells.

06:06.320 --> 06:07.430
Just miracles.

06:07.430 --> 06:07.940
Right.

06:07.940 --> 06:08.700
Okay.

06:10.100 --> 06:12.410
O sickle wings of the velociraptor...

06:12.410 --> 06:14.880
Slice, fly, and hunt!

06:18.330 --> 06:20.390
O merciful Earth Mother,

06:20.390 --> 06:24.480
please protect us, the weak, 
with the powers of the earth.

06:24.740 --> 06:25.690
Let's go.

06:32.750 --> 06:33.780
That's one.

06:37.020 --> 06:37.870
That's two.

06:38.150 --> 06:41.050
O Great Sheep who walked the Cretaceous...

06:41.050 --> 06:46.760
Grant to us a modicum of your 
long-sung success in battle!

06:49.810 --> 06:53.680
Damn it. I've seen more goblins 
than I want to in a whole lifetime.

06:53.680 --> 06:55.600
You sure are cheerful, Scaly.

06:57.170 --> 07:00.310
Over there! There's one with a 
weird-looking staff over there!

07:02.480 --> 07:04.330
A shaman? That's eight.

07:04.330 --> 07:05.400
Can you take it out?

07:05.680 --> 07:07.320
I'll give it a try.

07:07.440 --> 07:08.560
Take that!

07:25.570 --> 07:29.650
O merciful Earth Mother, please bless us,

07:29.650 --> 07:31.760
the wanderers in the 
darkness, with holy light!

07:40.130 --> 07:41.950
All right! You're mine!

08:02.970 --> 08:04.010
Crap!

08:04.010 --> 08:06.160
Keep your senses about you!

08:10.430 --> 08:12.770
<i>It feels like I'm underwater.</i>

08:16.680 --> 08:18.060
Goblin Slayer!

08:19.860 --> 08:20.930
Everyone!

08:32.680 --> 08:33.550
<i>No...</i>

08:45.150 --> 08:46.420
Impure.

08:47.410 --> 08:49.750
O merciful Earth Mother,

08:49.750 --> 08:53.420
please, by your revered hand, 
cleanse us of our corruption.

08:53.970 --> 08:55.190
Purify!

09:17.440 --> 09:18.210
Huh?

09:28.640 --> 09:29.530
Huh?

09:36.090 --> 09:39.840
What... What have I done?

09:46.840 --> 09:48.160
Well done.

09:50.450 --> 09:51.570
Well done.

09:56.020 --> 09:57.740
R-Right...

09:58.500 --> 09:59.300
Good.

10:09.070 --> 10:10.570
That's nineteen. Stand up.

10:13.130 --> 10:14.930
O-Orcbolg...

10:14.930 --> 10:15.750
Drink this.

10:17.000 --> 10:17.950
Use this!

10:21.110 --> 10:23.060
I'm all good over here, Beard-cutter.

10:25.090 --> 10:27.920
Sir Goblin Slayer, let us regroup.

10:27.920 --> 10:28.940
Thanks.

10:32.290 --> 10:34.290
Goblin Slayer...

10:34.290 --> 10:35.450
You did well.

10:39.230 --> 10:41.180
R-Right...

10:42.770 --> 10:49.000
Gorgosaurus, beautiful though wounded,
may I partake in the healing of your body!

10:53.170 --> 10:54.260
We're moving ahead.

10:54.570 --> 10:55.420
Can you run?

10:55.420 --> 10:57.490
I'm fine. Come on, let's go.

10:57.490 --> 10:59.740
Yes. I can also go.

11:00.340 --> 11:01.340
I will go!

11:04.370 --> 11:05.640
That's twenty-two.

11:05.850 --> 11:09.100
Sir Spellcaster, are you ready?

11:09.450 --> 11:13.520
You bet. Considering all the 
trouble we went through for this.

11:15.170 --> 11:16.200
That's twenty-four.

11:22.920 --> 11:23.860
Jump!

11:28.140 --> 11:33.290
Spin the buckets, gnomes! 
Make them spin and spin and let them go!

11:35.010 --> 11:37.130
Falling Control...

11:37.130 --> 11:39.760
It was good that you saved that spell for me.

11:39.760 --> 11:41.260
I know what I'm doing.

11:43.000 --> 11:44.140
You okay?

11:44.370 --> 11:46.090
This went well.

11:46.090 --> 11:48.600
I wasn't so sure how things 
would end up for a moment.

11:49.110 --> 11:50.060
Yeah.

11:51.820 --> 11:55.020
This is the best way to 
take care of the goblins.

12:24.540 --> 12:26.580
I-Is that going to be okay?

12:26.580 --> 12:30.240
The hole made to the fortress 
on the embankment using

12:30.240 --> 12:32.210
the Tunnel spell will eventually close up.

12:32.210 --> 12:33.780
This building won't be destroyed.

12:33.780 --> 12:36.400
That's not what I meant. 
I'm talking about the water that's inside.

12:37.100 --> 12:38.580
I can't do anything about that.

12:38.580 --> 12:42.290
We'll just have to let the elves 
know later to deal with it.

12:43.240 --> 12:45.570
And once we get back, 
there's a wedding to go to.

12:48.880 --> 12:51.490
You haven't thought about marriage yourself?

12:51.490 --> 12:53.540
Not for another thousand years, at least.

12:53.540 --> 12:54.680
That might be too late.

12:54.680 --> 12:55.870
What'd you say?!

12:56.400 --> 13:01.260
Once I become a dragon, 
may I take you as a dragon's bride?

13:01.260 --> 13:04.720
Wait, what? Are you asking me out? Seriously?

13:04.720 --> 13:09.450
Well, we'll just have to 
see in a thousand years.

13:11.910 --> 13:12.880
Are you tired?

13:12.880 --> 13:16.550
Oh, no. I'm not... but maybe a little.

13:16.550 --> 13:17.540
I see.

13:20.060 --> 13:24.930
<i>Will I be able to continue believing 
in the great Earth Mother?</i>

13:25.740 --> 13:30.540
<i>Am I worthy of receiving miracles 
from the great Earth Mother?</i>

13:32.000 --> 13:37.740
<i>Have I been able to grow even 
a little from a year ago?</i>

13:38.340 --> 13:38.950
Look.

13:38.950 --> 13:39.790
Huh?

13:40.900 --> 13:41.750
A rainbow.

14:00.360 --> 14:02.820
Dawn Strike!

14:04.780 --> 14:06.780
Hell! It's hell!

14:10.450 --> 14:13.490
Carbunculus... Crescunt... Iacta!

14:17.840 --> 14:21.590
I can keep going, but how are 
the rest of you holding up?

14:22.680 --> 14:25.420
It's... probably going 
to take a little longer.

14:27.030 --> 14:29.890
The flow of water has changed above.

14:30.440 --> 14:32.860
It seems our opponent's 
magic circle has broken.

14:32.860 --> 14:34.350
Sealing them again will be easier now.

14:34.350 --> 14:38.060
Huh? I wonder if there were 
other adventurers around.

14:38.720 --> 14:41.560
The gate to Hell is about to open.

14:42.420 --> 14:44.870
We connected somewhere forbidden...

14:45.410 --> 14:48.530
We opened the gate to transfer us to Hell.

14:49.180 --> 14:51.490
Though it has been sealed,

14:52.230 --> 14:54.470
the gate will eventually open again.

14:55.270 --> 14:57.830
Considering that timing 
is apparently right now...

14:57.830 --> 15:00.460
I can't tell if my luck is good or bad.

15:00.700 --> 15:02.140
Maybe it's the elves.

15:02.140 --> 15:03.490
I'm not so sure.

15:03.860 --> 15:05.920
They're slow to act, so I'm not sure if

15:05.920 --> 15:08.390
they'd bother to take action 
at such an opportune time.

15:08.750 --> 15:10.460
When an elf points,

15:10.460 --> 15:14.220
their hand can pierce through vital points 
at the most unexpected angles.

15:15.100 --> 15:16.720
Well, whatever!

15:17.070 --> 15:20.240
Once we beat all these guys, 
everything will be solved!

15:22.540 --> 15:24.820
Here we go!

15:38.290 --> 15:41.460
And now, if you would exchange your vows.

15:45.930 --> 15:52.780
Usamiakitowotoku riinomochinneie 
inoyurun'ahowo chihionokahisatawa.

15:53.450 --> 16:00.850
Usamiakitowotoku oshiroyuinawoto 
kisototowo chihionokahisatawa.

16:08.510 --> 16:11.240
Did you hear the blessings from the forest?

16:11.690 --> 16:12.490
Yes.

16:12.490 --> 16:13.450
Yes.

16:13.450 --> 16:14.240
Then...

16:28.690 --> 16:30.700
Their vows have been exchanged!

16:31.230 --> 16:34.640
A new forest will be born
 where that arrow lands.

16:35.210 --> 16:38.650
Tonight shall be regarded as 
the moonlit night in which

16:38.650 --> 16:40.930
the rainbow appeared for centuries to come.

16:50.700 --> 16:54.090
So what happened when you were 
caught in the goblins' trap?

16:54.090 --> 16:59.660
W-Well, me and long-ear— 
I mean, your princess—were about to—

16:59.660 --> 17:04.120
I'm sorry for all the trouble 
our princess must be causing you.

17:04.120 --> 17:05.980
No, no, not at all.

17:05.980 --> 17:08.170
She's actually rather quick-witted.

17:10.840 --> 17:13.790
Hey, Scaly! Give me a hand real quick!

17:13.790 --> 17:15.510
What is the matter, Sir Spellcaster?

17:15.910 --> 17:19.640
I can't handle all of them on my own.

17:19.640 --> 17:21.470
Well, well, in that case...

17:22.030 --> 17:26.600
Elves, how about I tell you the 
tale of the greatest lizardman,

17:26.600 --> 17:30.050
the one with black scales 
who could summon storms?

17:30.050 --> 17:32.900
Oh, hey, I know of him. 
I've met him before.

17:34.580 --> 17:41.550
Then I hope you enjoy the truth and 
legends of a century and millennium ago.

17:45.130 --> 17:48.540
Yeah, Elder Sister is definitely embarrassed.

17:49.540 --> 17:51.190
You don't need to go?

17:52.500 --> 17:53.800
This is your home, isn't it?

17:53.800 --> 17:55.810
Oh, nah. It's no big deal.

17:55.810 --> 17:58.290
For them, to put it in human terms,

17:58.290 --> 18:01.720
it'd only feel like I was 
away for two or three days.

18:01.720 --> 18:02.620
I see.

18:02.980 --> 18:06.770
My sister did say she'd write me
once things settled down.

18:09.250 --> 18:10.650
Why don't you write a letter?

18:10.960 --> 18:13.100
You haven't been back to 
your homeland, have you?

18:13.640 --> 18:15.570
No one would read a letter from me.

18:16.280 --> 18:19.280
I'm an incompetent younger brother.

18:19.940 --> 18:23.230
Is that so? I honestly think 
you're doing a good job.

18:23.230 --> 18:25.250
You're even silver-ranked.

18:25.900 --> 18:26.900
I see.

18:28.260 --> 18:29.220
I see...

18:29.920 --> 18:33.750
Seriously, Orcbolg. 
All you ever say is, "I see."

18:35.610 --> 18:36.490
Are you going?

18:37.260 --> 18:40.930
A girl has her own ways of having fun.

18:41.660 --> 18:42.490
I'm glad...

18:43.190 --> 18:46.520
I'm glad your sister was able to get married.

18:47.970 --> 18:49.350
Thanks.

18:52.950 --> 18:55.650
What's the matter? You seem down.

18:55.650 --> 18:58.030
Oh, no. I'm fine...

18:58.030 --> 18:59.310
Don't lie to me.

19:00.050 --> 19:01.400
It doesn't matter what it is.

19:01.400 --> 19:03.570
If you've got something pent up, just say it.

19:03.570 --> 19:05.460
We're here to celebrate today.

19:05.460 --> 19:09.500
Then what do the vows they 
exchanged earlier mean, exactly?

19:09.880 --> 19:15.030
Oh, that? They just basically 
swore they'd be together forever.

19:15.470 --> 19:18.750
Of course, that's forever in elf terms.

19:19.180 --> 19:20.740
Will you say a prayer?

19:20.740 --> 19:22.680
A prayer?

19:22.940 --> 19:25.180
Yeah, to the Earth Mother.

19:25.180 --> 19:29.300
Elves do have some ties 
with her, too, you know.

19:30.100 --> 19:31.300
Very well.

19:34.950 --> 19:42.340
O merciful Earth Mother, please, by your 
revered hand, may all their paths bear good fruit.

19:54.130 --> 19:56.830
It looks like my prayer 
reached the Earth Mother.

19:58.000 --> 20:00.170
Now my sister will be all set.

20:00.840 --> 20:01.770
Yes.

20:03.870 --> 20:05.980
In that case, come on. Let's go.

20:05.980 --> 20:07.080
Huh?

20:09.300 --> 20:12.230
Hey, you two! Over here!

20:14.460 --> 20:17.150
You know, I'm really nervous.

20:17.150 --> 20:19.820
I've never been to a party like this before.

20:19.820 --> 20:22.850
Confidence is the key.
Just be confident.

20:22.850 --> 20:25.050
Oh? I guess you're used to these occasions?

20:25.050 --> 20:27.160
I was trained for these at home.

20:27.160 --> 20:31.710
Not to mention, there are parties 
like this in my line of work.

20:31.710 --> 20:34.560
Huh... Well, whatever.

20:34.560 --> 20:37.540
Hey, look! Let's head up front.

20:39.180 --> 20:41.150
What's about to start?

20:41.150 --> 20:43.090
You'll see in a sec.

20:43.790 --> 20:47.570
Oh, is this the gift from the bride?

20:47.570 --> 20:49.690
Oh, I've heard of that before!

20:49.690 --> 20:52.890
They say the person who receives 
it will be able to get married.

20:52.890 --> 20:55.280
I've helped out at a ceremony before.

20:55.720 --> 20:59.720
If she's gonna hand it out, 
it'd be a shame not to take it.

20:59.720 --> 21:01.320
Huh...

21:05.410 --> 21:08.180
Never hold back at times like these.

21:08.180 --> 21:09.660
Oh, r-right.

21:10.880 --> 21:13.830
Love is fate. Fate is death.

21:16.920 --> 21:21.880
Then may the next love and affection 
go to the maidens fated for death.

21:44.360 --> 21:49.170
<i>We then had fun for three days and three 
nights before returning to the town.</i>

21:50.060 --> 21:54.910
<i>Quite a bit of time has passed since, 
but my sister's letter still hasn't reached me.</i>

21:56.000 --> 22:00.670
<i>Which probably means that their 
banquet still continues today.</i>

23:32.010 --> 23:40.250
<b>Next Time</b>

23:32.010 --> 23:40.250
<b>Once There Was Youth, Now There Is Nothing but Ash</b>
